  "family": "vits",
  "note": "Measured across all three Quantization Profiles on CPU and CUDA, over the twelve\ncommitted Port Validation Cases of the vits-ljspeech Reference Model Variant.\nNumerical acceptance thresholds and perceptual quality evaluation remain\ndeferred; no placeholder tolerance or quality score is claimed.\n\nThis file previously carried an empty `stages` object with the measurements\ndescribed only in prose. That was not a formatting detail. Because\ntests/python/test_tolerance_coverage.py skips families with no recorded grid,\nthis family had no cross-check between what the package claims and what was\nactually run, and on 2026-07-26 that let a real defect ship silently: removing\nthe CUDA strict-FP32 gate changed duration.w_ceil on the 315-token case, moving\nthe frame count by one hop, and nothing failed. It was found by comparing CPU\nagainst CUDA by hand. Recording the grid is what closes that hole, and the check\nwas verified to bite by deleting a stage and watching it fail.\n\nThe structural probes are the guarantee that has to hold across backends, and\nthey hold: duration.w_ceil, duration.y_length and duration.attention are exact on\nevery case, every profile and both backends. That is not free -- the stage\nproducing them runs on CPU on every backend, for the reason recorded in\ndocs/porting/families/vits.md. The duration-path slice reports no worst-case\ndrift because there is none to rank: its probes are integers compared for\nequality, so its entries carry exact_on_every_case rather than a measured\nmaximum.\n\nTwo limits of this file, stated rather than implied. It covers vits-ljspeech\nonly; vits-vctk is a second Reference Model Variant with its own twelve cases and\nits own speaker-conditioned path, and the coverage test keys on family rather\nthan variant, so vctk remains unchecked by that test. And CUDA drift is measured\nagainst the CPU oracle while CUDA F32 matrix multiplies compute at TF32\nprecision, so the intermediate figures mix implementation difference with\nprecision difference; see docs/backends.md.",
